{"title":"Successor set","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b88e2f3749515db6b27b6b4dd0b4f649278a447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\subset \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> is called a <b>successor set</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Iff\" title=\"Iff\">iff</a>\n</p>\n<dl><dd>(i) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c9992f0534616f1e778341c161452f2aabd249ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>(ii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fabcbe6ca465d938f42d3b2421fe03cd66e3a52d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall n\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9be6f7ae2670d327312a92eb498cf6b5c8f39f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>The set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Natural_number\" title=\"Natural number\">natural numbers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the <i>smallest</i> successor set, as for any successor set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07c7578c674f57baccf1b8c5948161a75a655af6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N} \\subset S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295a5880948cadf1f4eecb5cf96b9c1caedcf4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}=\\{1,2,3\\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> is not the only successor set. For example, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/736ee6214032f472832c7c622915e3ff61584199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\{1,\\sqrt{2},2,1+\\sqrt{2},\\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" /> is also a successor set.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Successor_set&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018111322\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 34/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 280/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1672/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.237      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.237      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6323:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018111322 and revision id 22803. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}